  "question": {
    "text": "In an acid-base titration, <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> solution was added to the <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> solution of unknown strength. Which of the following correctly shown the change of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> of the titration mixture in this experiment?<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0092_7dd06d012bbe.png\" style=\"width: 499px; height: 424px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For titration of strong base with strong acid <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> changes sharply near equivalence point and at equivalent point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> sharply decreases because strong base &amp; strong acid dissociate completely.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mover><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi>aCl</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math><br />at equivalent point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math> and at endpoint solution will be neutral."
